From 68934ae9b1e65d46f8fcb09e0eb3e705d7554dd5 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: TofuJoe <darryl.hon@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 14 Sep 2026 21:15:19 -0600
Subject: [PATCH 14/32] drm/xe/display: Pool DSB buffers and skip unchanged DPT
 rewrites

On an external DP output each commit created and destroyed a DSB command
buffer BO (~71 us + ~38 us measured at 5K). Pool up to four released DSB
BOs; a reused one is cleared.

At 5K each flip also cleared and rewrote the ~17k-entry DPT of a pooled BO
(~110 us). Pool entries now remember the fb BO backing generation, PTE
flags and GTT view they were written for; when the same key is pinned
again the pooled DPT is used as is. Any backing change of the fb BO renews
its generation, so a stale DPT is never reused.

The pool alignment check now matches the GGTT allocator, which aligns node
offsets relative to the GGTT start.

Assisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-5
